# US-422: real 404s for unknown URLs (fix soft 404).
#
# Cloudflare Pages resolution order: a Pages Function (functions/*) runs first,
# then an exact static-asset match (every prerendered public page —
# /, /pricing, /privacy, /grading/<slug>, … — is a dist/<route>/index.html file
# and is served directly), and only THEN are these _redirects rules evaluated.
#
# IMPORTANT: the client-rendered app shells (/dashboard, /admin, /auth/*,
# /login, /signup, /accept-invite) are NO LONGER served from here. A _redirects
# `→ /index.html 200` rewrite gets canonicalized by Cloudflare Pages into a
# 308 → / (which broke hard-loads / refreshes of every app route). Those
# namespaces are now served as 200 by dedicated Pages Functions
# (functions/dashboard/[[path]].ts, …, functions/_shared/spa-shell.ts) — wired
# in public/_routes.json — which run BEFORE this file. This rule only catches
# paths with NO function and NO static file → a real 404 (no soft-404 indexing).
# US-1680: short, shareable certificate alias. /c/<id> 301s to the canonical
# /cert/<id> (the cert SSR Pages Function + self-canonical), so sellers can share
# a compact link without splitting link equity across two indexable URLs.
/c/:id          /cert/:id     301

# US-9012: the flaw library moved from /grading/flaws to /care when it was
# reframed from disclosure-first to removal-first. Both rules are needed: the
# splat catches the 32 entry pages, the exact rule catches the hub, and a splat
# alone does not match the bare prefix.
#
# THESE MUST STAY ABOVE THE /* CATCH-ALL. This file is first-match-wins, so a
# rule placed after the 404 rule never runs. Written below it first, which would
# have 404'd every old flaw URL instead of redirecting it.
#
# 301 not 302: the move is permanent and the pages have ten weeks of history to
# carry across. src/test/care-redirects.test.ts asserts every live /care route
# has a rule pointing at it, so renaming a slug cannot silently orphan the old
# URL, and that the rules sit above the catch-all.
/grading/flaws          /care         301
/grading/flaws/*        /care/:splat  301

/*              /404.html     404
